  "heading": "\\intermediate.value.theorem",
  "heading_latex": "\\textrm{Intermediate Value Theorem}",
  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[\\intermediate.value.theorem]\nTheorem:\ngiven:\n. a, b is \\real\n. f is \\function:on{\\reals}:to{\\reals}\nwhere:\n. a \\:real.less?:/ b\nthen:\n. forAll: y is \\real\n  then:\n  . let: v is \\real\n    where:\n    . v = f(b)\n    . f(a) \\:real.less?:/ y\n    . y \\:real.less?:/ v\n    then:\n    . exists: c is \\real\n      suchThat:\n      . a \\:real.less?:/ c\n      . c \\:real.less?:/ b\n      . f(c) = y\nDocumented:\n. called: \"Intermediate Value Theorem\"\n. description: \"A continuous function on an interval attains every intermediate\n                value between its endpoints.\"\nId: \"f29c7f02-8e4f-46da-ac4e-3df62dca57f0\"",
